    },
    {
      "id": "rk3y6cv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "6.1.2 RAM (Random Access Memory)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fogiu27",
      "content": "RAM is volatile memory, meaning its contents are lost when the power is turned off. It temporarily stores programs and data currently being used by the CPU."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z4g5y46",
      "content": "Types of RAM:"
    },
    {
      "id": "mjacxb6",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "DRAM – Dynamic RAM",
        "SRAM – Static RAM"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Primary Memory (Main Memory)",
      "id": "4it1yc2"
    },
    {
      "id": "d7h8f9s",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "6.1.3 ROM (Read Only Memory)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bkxv6w9",
      "content": "ROM is non-volatile memory used to store permanent instructions required for booting the computer."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t0d1q4m",
      "content": "Types of ROM:"
    },
    {
      "id": "478ndg6",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "PROM – Programmable Read Only Memory",
        "EPROM – Erasable Programmable ROM",
        "EEPROM – Electrically Erasable Programmable ROM"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "tqep8w4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "6.1.4 Cache Memory"
    },
